{
  "artwork": "Every button's backdrop rect is resolved from fit, zoom, offsetX and offsetY, all of which are ABSENT-IS-NOT-ZERO: a button with a source and none of the framing keys (conformance.press) resolves to fit \"contain\", zoom 1, offsetX 0, offsetY 0, opacity 1 - the same rect the box itself describes - never to a collapsed or invisible rect. zoom scales the artwork about its own centre; offsetX/offsetY are then applied as a fraction of the element's own width/height, which is what backdropOffsetX/backdropOffsetY show translated outside the zoom scale rather than folded into it. conformance.boundary and conformance.silent carry no source at all, so they have no backdrop entry here - there is nothing to resolve.",
  "ring": "conformance.full (borderStyle static + borderColor) and conformance.boundary (borderStyle hue-shift, no borderColor) each draw a ring at ringWidth 2.0 - identical at both bases. That is the profile's one length that is not a fraction of the basis: a ring that grew with the element would read inconsistently across differently sized widgets, so it is the deliberate exception to the halving rule everything else in this table follows. cornerRadius still scales with the element and halves normally. conformance.press and conformance.silent declare no borderStyle, so absence means no ring at all - never borderStyle \"static\" and never a ring in the reader's own colour.",
  "press": "Press feedback is the reader's own, painted without waiting for the producer: pressTintAlpha 0.2, pressFadeInMs 20, pressFadeOutMs 140 and pressMinVisibleMs 60 are constants, identical for every button at every basis - they are durations and an alpha, not lengths, so they are stated once here rather than repeated per node. pressSurface is the one part of this primitive a screenshot comparison would never catch: it is the element's WHOLE box, padding included, not the smaller area the label and artwork occupy - pressSurfaceWidth/pressSurfaceHeight below equal the node's own outer width/height for exactly that reason.",
  "label": "Each button's primary label is its first child text, resolved the same way conformance-slider-layout.json's header label is: fontSize from its own size, lines from maxLines (absent means 1, even when wrap is true), textAlign from the text's own align (absent means start), and blockAlign from the button's own align - the cross-axis placement the button gives its children, absent meaning stretch. conformance.full (align end) and conformance.press (align center) are the two extremes; a renderer conflating the button's own align with the label's textAlign cannot reproduce both from one fixture.",
